              { "do": "Substitute", "math": "\\displaystyle\\int t^4\\cdot\\dfrac{dt}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\dfrac{t^5}{5} + C = \\dfrac{t^5}{20} + C" },
              { "do": "Put back $t = \\sin(x^4)$ and compare", "math": "\\dfrac{1}{20}\\sin^5(x^4) + C \\;\\Rightarrow\\; a = \\dfrac{1}{20}", "marks": 1 }
            ],
            "mistake": "Forgetting the $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ from $d(x^4) = 4x^3\\,dx$ and choosing (D) $\\dfrac{1}{5}$."
          }
        },
        {
